####

1 - Understanding pod selector - 

1a. The below example will select any pods in the namespace production

---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: default-deny-ingress
  namespace: production 
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  
1b. The below example will select pods with label role = database
  
---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: default-deny-ingress
  namespace: production 
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      role: database
  
2 - policy Type - 
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: default-deny-ingress
  namespace: production 
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  
  policyTypes:
  - Ingress
  - Egress
  
  
Scenerio - Network policy to deny ingress/egress traffic for pods  in production namespace
---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: Example1
  namespace: production
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  policyTypes:
  - Ingress
  - Egress
  
Scenerio - Allow ingress but block Egress 

---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: Example2
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  ingress:
  - {}
  policyTypes:
  - Ingress
  - Egress
  
Scenerio - Blocks all ingress & egress to pod with role=suspicious
  
---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: Example3
spec:
  podSelector:
	matchLabels:
	  role: suspicious
  policyTypes:
  - Ingress
  - Egress
  
Scenerio 4 [ pod selector ] -All Pods with label of role=app to connect to pods with labels of role=database 

We have 3 pods - 
app-pod - role=app
db-pod - role=database
random-pod - role=random-pod
---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: example4
  namespace: default
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      role: database
  policyTypes:
  - Ingress
  ingress:
  - from:
    - podSelector:
        matchLabels:
          role: app


Scenerio 5 [ NameSpace selector ] - Allow pods from security namespace to connect to pods in prod namespace 

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: example5
  namespace: prod
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  ingress:
  - from:
    - namespaceSelector:
        matchLabels:
           kubernetes.io/metadata.name: security
  policyTypes:
  - Ingress

Scenerio 6  [ipBlock]- Allow pods from production namespace to connect to only 8.8.8.8 IP address outbound 

apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: example6
  namespace: production
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  
  egress:
  - to:
    - ipBlock:
        cidr: 8.8.8.8/32
  policyTypes:
  - Egress
